Z||000000||Cheever2||04-03-2001||01:47 PM||||...or vice versa.<P>Please try to find & post (or e-mail) a straight-on shot of the back end of the car, so I can paste it over my damaged GT.  I want to see what my Coupe rear bumper would look like on it, but my coupe is red, and changing the color with my software wouldn't look natural.  So I need a pic of a black car.<P>Also, Tigger, my search found you once said this: "Only difference between the GT and SE bumpers in the rear is the plastic bracket that buttons up the lower half of the GT's."  What bracket do you mean?<P>||||reg||12
Z||000001||Oreif||04-03-2001||02:06 PM||||An SE rear has the ribbed molding and the top is angled to meet the tail light assembly. The GT (fastback) is straighter since the tail lights go straight up and the molding is smooth. The only difference Tigger might be talking about is the 85 GT vs the 86/87 SE.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
